From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Reuse the effective range after clearing native views

The native-view recovery path passes the raw optional limits to the
second attempt instead of the effective range resolved by map_view().
Ordinary NtAllocateVirtualMemory() calls use zero for both optional
limits, leaving the retry with an empty range.

Retry with the effective start/end range calculated by map_view().
This allows 32-bit applications to recover after native mappings
are removed instead of returning STATUS_NO_MEMORY for every probe.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -2346,7 +2346,7 @@ static NTSTATUS map_view( struct file_view **view_ret, void *base, size_t size,
         WARN("Allocation failed, clearing native views.\n");
         clear_native_views();
         if (!is_win64) increase_try_map_step = FALSE;
-        ptr = map_free_area( (void *)limit_low, (void *)limit_high, host_size, top_down, unix_prot,
+        ptr = map_free_area( start, end, host_size, top_down, unix_prot,
                                align_mask );
         if (!is_win64) increase_try_map_step = TRUE;
         if (!ptr) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
--
2.53.0
